You're right that being stunned makes it much harder to engrave Elbereth
or aim wands probably. It *is* a minor trouble, though, that can be fixed
by prayer as long as (AFAIK) you don't have any worse problems (e.g.
hunger, blindness, ...). Applying a (non-cursed) unicorn horn also cures 
that problem but at that point of the game you probably don't have any.

The main task for you seems to be to *avoid* being stunned. That means that
eating any kind of bat or yellow molds is a big no-no because stunning is 
about the only thing they confer.
Booby trapped doors are a problem, I agree, but if you remember to #untrap
any door you see there is a good chance to remove those annoying traps 
before they explode in your face. Or you might let other monsters open them
but this is not very practical.

